.TH LLM-MANAGER-RESTORE-EXECUTE 8 "2026-09-06" "LLM-Manager" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
llm-manager-restore-execute \- execute one approved fixed-target system restore
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pkexec /usr/bin/llm-manager-restore-execute
.I request-sha256 canonical-request-hex
.SH DESCRIPTION
This dedicated privileged entry executes one previously saved, unexpired and
unused LLM-Manager local root restore review for the fixed Ollama drop-in.
It independently verifies caller identity, host, request, review, encrypted
root-owned backup, current target, expiry and immutable execution history.
.PP
The canonical request is limited to 16 KiB before lowercase hexadecimal
encoding and contains metadata only. It does not contain settings plaintext.
The operation records an attempt before mutation, holds the shared target lock,
restores one fixed file, reloads and restarts the fixed Ollama unit, validates
the service, and persists a terminal result. It never retries automatically.
.SH SECURITY
This command requires the dedicated execute-system-restore PolicyKit action.
Authentication for review or ordinary Apply is not execution authority.
All stores, keys, audit directories and the target parent must already exist
with safe root ownership and permissions; this command does not provision them.
.PP
If execution is interrupted or reported as unconfirmed, do not invoke it again.
Use the read-only status command of llm-manager-restore-review with the exact
request ID and SHA-256. Missing or incomplete evidence is not proof that no
mutation occurred.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 means a terminal result was persisted; inspect its state because it may be
failed or unknown. 1 means rejected, unavailable or unconfirmed execution and
must not be treated as safe to retry. 2 indicates invalid CLI syntax.
